{"path": "Checkpoints/jm-v0-waves-green-a39afe8/src/verbs/filter.ts", "category": "bug", "severity": "high", "content": "The worker has no try/catch around `judge.ask()` + `budget.spend()`, unlike decision-tree.ts (lines 56-69). Non-JEV_NO_KEY errors — including `JM_BUDGET_EXCEEDED` from the check-then-act TOCTOU (multiple lanes pass `roomLeft()` before any `spend()` runs) and network/transport errors from `judge.ask()` — fall into runPool's `errors` array, where only `JEV_NO_KEY` is inspected. All other errors are silently swallowed: the candidate is dropped from `rows` (neither kept nor rejected), `budgetStopped` stays `false` (the throw happens after the `roomLeft()` check), and no indication surfaces. Mirror decision-tree.ts: wrap in try/catch, re-throw JEV_NO_KEY, and reject errored candidates (p=0, keep=false, error reason) so they're visible rather than silently lost.", "existing_code": "const res = await judge.ask({ candidate: { path: c.path, size: c.size, excerpt } },
      { match: { type: "noul", instructions: opts.question } }, "is-x@v1");
    const p = (res.answers.match as { noul?: number })?.noul ?? 0;
    if (!res.cached) { calls++; costUsd += res.costUsd; }
    budget.spend(res.costUsd);
    const keep = p >= minP;
    rows.push({ path: c.path, size: c.size, p, keep, reason: keep ? "kept" : `p<${minP}`, cached: res.cached });
    return rows[rows.length - 1];", "suggestion_code": "try {
